(Evaluating a structured digital platform with nursing support for reducing dietary sodium) Tj
T*
(in kidney disease: a protocol for implementation science research) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Excessive dietary sodium intake accelerates renal disease progression and hypertension in) Tj
T*
(patients with chronic kidney disease. While evidence-based education can improve dietary) Tj
T*
(awareness, adoption of sustainable behavioral change remains challenging. This mixed-) Tj
T*
(methods implementation study will evaluate a technology-enhanced nursing intervention) Tj
T*
(designed to support sodium restriction in patients with stages 3-4 chronic kidney disease.) Tj
T*
(The protocol combines quantitative measures \(24-hour urinary sodium as primary endpoint,) Tj
T*
(blood pressure, and knowledge assessments\) with qualitative interviews exploring) Tj
T*
(facilitators and barriers to engagement. Approximately 100 participants will be randomized) Tj
T*
(1:1 to receive either enhanced digital coaching with nurse-led support or usual care) Tj
T*
(comparator. Data collection spans 12 months. Mixed-methods analysis will integrate) Tj
T*
(quantitative outcomes with qualitative findings to identify implementation factors) Tj
T*
(influencing behavior change and inform future scaling.) Tj
